@ Start

$ Background {&/Game/Melodia/UI/Textures/Figma/T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_SakuraDream.T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_SakuraDream} none 0

- Melusina
  The festival banners are already down. Someone else packed the last cart before the dew even dried.
  The road is kind like that—it always lets you be just a little too late.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_road_01.mel_road_01} 0.9

- Melusina
  And the bedside perch is empty again. It is impressive how a small absence can take up an entire room.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_perch_01.mel_perch_01} 0.9

- .
  Across the courtyard, the four brass-inlaid doors of the Morning House stand sealed. Every key-plate along the wall hums with an unfinished bar of music—four measures left behind when the choir departed for the Sea Above.

- Melusina
  Sir flew off for snacks again. Or to audit the roof tiles. He always comes back when the kettle gives up.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_snackrun_01.mel_snackrun_01} 0.9

- .
  A sharp, bright chirp rings from the window arch, seven semitones above the fountain's murmur.

      $ SFX {&/Game/Audio/Aud_Source/fx_Amb_SoundScape/Birds/amb_ss_palette_bird01_mid_01.amb_ss_palette_bird01_mid_01} 0.85

* Answer the chirp with a fifth on the WaveHarp. | melodia_met_melodious = on | -> Reunion
* Wait by the fountain and let him finish the phrase. | -> Listening

<@> Reunion

? if: {melodia_met_melodious} == on

  - Melusina
    There. A clean fifth. I can answer the room without pretending it's full.

        $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_reunion_01.mel_reunion_01} 0.9
        $ SFX {&/Game/Melodia/Audio/WaveHarp/SW_WaveHarp_Orchestra_C4.SW_WaveHarp_Orchestra_C4} 0.75

  - Sir Melodious
    A touch sharp on the attack, little bard, but the courtyard forgives you. I was not foraging—I was inspecting the locks.

  - Melusina
    The house locked itself.

  - Sir Melodious
    The house is an instrument, Melusina. When the choir sailed for the high tide without playing the closing cadence, all four chambers sealed on the rest.

? else:

  - Melusina
    I will listen first. The answer can come when the echo has made room for it.

? endif

-> Departure

<@> Listening

- Melusina
  I'll let him have the downbeat. If you rush a bird, he lectures you about tempo for three miles.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_halfsong_01.mel_halfsong_01} 0.9

- Sir Melodious
  I heard that! And it was four miles, because you were dragging the third measure.

      $ SFX {&/Game/Audio/Aud_Source/fx_Amb_SoundScape/Birds/amb_ss_palette_bird01_mid_03.amb_ss_palette_bird01_mid_03} 0.85

- Melusina
  Morning, Sir. Why are the four inner chambers sealed?

- Sir Melodious
  Because a house built on resonance does not open to iron keys. It opens to the four measures the festival left behind: an Echo, a Seam, a Chorister, and the Tide Above.

-> Departure

<@> Departure

- Melusina
  I'll keep the seat warm. Arriving late isn't the same as being unwanted—it just means we get the quiet part of the score to ourselves.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_arrival_01.mel_arrival_01} 0.9

- Sir Melodious
  Then bring your WaveHarp. Something restless has knotted itself around the first measure out in the sanctuary.

- Melusina
  The dream is restless. Stay close, and sing when I sing.

      $ Voice {&/Game/Melodia/Characters/Melusina/Audio/mel_battle_entry.mel_battle_entry} 0.9

$ Notify melodia:flag:melodia_smoke_complete:true

$ %melodia_morning_sir.BeginWindowDeparture
$ End
